# Studio Frontend Quality Standard

## 1. Visual & Token Discipline
- Never invent ad-hoc hex colors, arbitrary spacing, or random border radii. Map all styling to semantic CSS variables / Tailwind theme tokens defined in `DESIGN.md`.
- Establish clear typographic contrast: pair a distinct display/heading treatment with highly legible body copy (`tabular-nums` for numeric data, balanced line lengths `55ch–70ch`).
- Avoid AI clichés: no gratuitous purple-blue gradients, no glowing neon drop-shadows on generic SaaS cards, no single-word rainbow headline highlights, and no placeholder copy ("Lorem ipsum", "John Doe").

## 2. Motion & Scroll Choreography
- Purpose over decoration: every animation must clarify spatial origin, hierarchy, or state feedback.
- UI micro-interactions (modals, dropdowns, tabs, hover states) must be interruptible, stay under 300ms, and use `ease-out` for entrances (`cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`) and `ease-in-out` for layout shifts.
- Animate ONLY compositor-friendly properties (`transform`, `opacity`, `clip-path`). Never animate `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`, or `margin`.
- UI state motion: prefer Emil `/animate` (CSS/Motion). Scroll scrubbing, pinning, complex timelines: GSAP (`/gsap-scrolltrigger`, `/gsap-react`) with `useGSAP()` / `gsap.context()` cleanup.
- Respect `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` across both CSS and GSAP/Motion timelines.

## 3. Interaction & State Completeness
- Every interactive control must implement `:hover`, `:focus-visible`, `:active`, and `disabled` states.
- Never ship dead buttons or mock handlers. Every route, drawer, form submission, loading skeleton, empty state, and error recovery path must function end-to-end.

## 4. Engineering Hygiene
- Use compound component composition rather than prop-drilling 10+ boolean flags.
- Clean up all event listeners, `IntersectionObserver` instances, Lenis RAF loops, and GSAP contexts (`useGSAP` / `ctx.revert()`) on unmount.
